WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.342
C++ 26 is

00:00:02.154 --> 00:00:03.026
done again

00:00:03.558 --> 00:00:04.583
At the six-day

00:00:04.395 --> 00:00:05.586
meeting in Búzios

00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:06.199
Brazil

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.614
the committee adopted

00:00:07.438 --> 00:00:08.404
an extension to

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:09.607
contracts and wrote

00:00:09.419 --> 00:00:10.798
a detailed rationale

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.883
for national bodies

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:13.286
then recompleted the

00:00:13.098 --> 00:00:14.183
technical work

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:15.735
As I reported

00:00:15.547 --> 00:00:16.266
in March

00:00:16.337 --> 00:00:17.941
the ISO C++

00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:18.884
committee completed

00:00:18.696 --> 00:00:19.839
technical work on

00:00:19.651 --> 00:00:21.372
C++ 26

00:00:21.444 --> 00:00:22.174
at our March

00:00:21.986 --> 00:00:22.552
meeting

00:00:22.752 --> 00:00:23.566
following that

00:00:23.743 --> 00:00:24.368
we held the

00:00:24.179 --> 00:00:25.287
first meeting of

00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:26.785
C++ 29 in

00:00:26.597 --> 00:00:27.174
June

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.476
We had about

00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:29.879
220 attendees

00:00:30.045 --> 00:00:32.957
split about 35%/65%

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:34.526
in-person / remote-Zoom

00:00:34.727 --> 00:00:35.941
formally representing

00:00:35.752 --> 00:00:37.108
27 nations

00:00:37.638 --> 00:00:38.652
Full story on

00:00:38.463 --> 00:00:39.359
the dashboard
